	(text "1. Board 50 mm wide (Hammond 1455C slot), 120 mm length (1455C1202), 4\n    layers, 90 Ω differential pairs.\n2. ALL COPPER PULLED BACK ≥1 mm (target 2 mm) FROM BOTH LONG EDGES, every\n    layer, full length. The extrusion's aluminium slots grip those edges;\n    edge copper lets the enclosure short GND1 to GND2.\n3. ESD arrays (U2, U3) within 5 mm of the connector pins they protect. Array\n    GND pin on its own via straight to plane, never daisy-chained. Pair\n    routed in-line through pins 1/3 → 6/4, no stubs.\n4. Barrier: ≥8.3 mm creepage at U1, routed slot under T1, CY1 the only other\n    crossing. No copper bridges the barrier on any layer.\n5. ADuM4165 bypass caps within 10 mm total lead length.\n6. J1 and J2 end-launched, mating faces flush with the outer face of the\n    plastic end panels.\n7. Rectifier + LDO + TPS2553 zone measures 19.36 mm (20 mm budget). D1 and\n    D2 must be placed side by side, not in series; in series the zone\n    overruns by 3.36 mm.\n8. U1 (ADuM4165) pins 4, 7 (GND1) and 15, 16, 17 (GND2) are ground-only -- NOT\n    suitable for bypass capacitance (datasheet Table 12, p.12). C4/C5 bypass\n    returns to GND1 via pins 2/10 ONLY; VBUS2/VDD2 bypass returns to GND2 via\n    pins 11/19 ONLY -- never pins 4/7/15/16/17.\n9. VBUS_HOST's 4 caps serve 2 ICs -- see each cap's Description property\n    before placing. C6+C7 cluster at U4 pin 2 / T1 center-tap (C7 = SN6505B's\n    mandatory ≥4.7 µF VCC bypass, Table 5-1). C4 clusters at U1 pin 1\n    (ADuM4165 VBUS1 bypass, item 5's budget) -- NOT with C3. C3 is\n    J1-entrance bulk/inrush capacitance and stays near J1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 335.5 199.39 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "10e80524-dcd9-424b-8b95-82303e057849")
	)
